= The Countryside

A third of Germans live on the land, and the party barely reaches them. East of the Elbe, farm labourers work the Junkers' estates for a pittance and a cottage they can be thrown out of. In the south, the priests tell the smallholders that communists will take their cows. [? if inflation >= 40 : Inflation has paid off the farmers' debts, and they will not sell grain for paper. ?]

- @labourers: Organise the estate labourers for a harvest strike.
- @smallholders: Defend the smallholders against debt and requisition.
- @easy_discard

@labourers
subtitle: The estates of Saxony and Halle stop at harvest time. The landowners call out the civil guards.
on-arrival: {!
RG.district('halle', {militancy: 5, members: 0.04});
RG.district('saxony', {militancy: 3});
Q.repression += 3;
Q.civil_guards_strength += 5;
!}

The labourers strike for wages in money, not in potatoes. The landowners' guards come out with rifles.

@smallholders
subtitle: Patient work in the villages of Bavaria and Thuringia.
on-arrival: {!
RG.district('bavaria', {members: 0.08, loyalty: 3});
RG.district('thuringia', {members: 0.05});
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
!}

No forced requisitions, cheap credit, and the burden of the war on the rich: our programme for the villages is short, and some of the villagers read it.
